{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 170,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the biggest secrets of physics is that\nwe still don't fundamentally understand what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4160,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "happens when the smallest things interact\nwith big things - that is, when quantum mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8610,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meets our everyday world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10440,
    "dDurationMs": 3489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You've probably heard of the \"Schrodinger's\nCat\" experiment where a particle (in this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13929,
    "dDurationMs": 5091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "case a cat) is in a superposition of two states\n(both dead and alive) at once, until it interacts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19020,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the outside world - normally a photon\nof light that we send in to see what's going"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22590,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on (but it could also just be a random particle\nthat has nothing to do with us)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26330,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Upon interaction with the outside world, the\ncat is observed as being either dead, or alive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31210,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not both."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32210,
    "dDurationMs": 4309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is, physics can't explain how\nthe cat, or particle, goes from being in a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36519,
    "dDurationMs": 4421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combination of two states at once to being\nin \"just one\", or \"just the other\"; nor do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40940,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we know how the \"decision\" is made."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43440,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This isn't just a problem with cats, either\n- it plagues every single quantum mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47620,
    "dDurationMs": 4489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experiment, famous or otherwise, from the\ndouble slit experiment and quantum teleportation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52109,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the Stern-Gerlach experiment and tests\nof the Bell inequalities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55639,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In every case, we can predict how likely it\nis for a particle to be in one state or another,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59969,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but have no clue how it actually ends up that\nway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62539,
    "dDurationMs": 4391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's where the many-worlds picture of quantum\nmechanics comes in - basically, \"many-worlds\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66930,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proposes the idea that the quantum system\ndoesn't actually decide - rather, at every"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71440,
    "dDurationMs": 4139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "junction where large everyday stuff interacts\nwith a quantum system, the timeline of history"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75579,
    "dDurationMs": 3621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "splits and both possibilities happen on different,\nalternate branches."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79200,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, a choose-your-own-adventure where\nevery possible story happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83540,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this scenario, we'd think that only one\npossibility happened because we'd be stuck"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86850,
    "dDurationMs": 3659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on one of the branches, in a version of ourselves\nthat only sees one possibility happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90509,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In some ways, this sounds pretty fishy - I\nmean, it's hard to test the reality of a universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94909,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that hides its true nature from us by not\nallowing us to test or observe its true nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99329,
    "dDurationMs": 3871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But anyway, in the many-worlds picture of\nquantum mechanics, \"branch-points\" are predicted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103200,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to happen all the time, everywhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105270,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pretty much any time subatomic particles interact\nwith each other, or with anything else, anywhere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109619,
    "dDurationMs": 2511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the universe, there are multiple possible\noutcomes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112130,
    "dDurationMs": 2239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which means a LOT of branching of history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114369,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There may even be infinitely many branches."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116429,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So is the Many Worlds hypothesis true?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118689,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't know - it hasn't yet been tested\nexperimentally."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121619,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a bit of mathematics that supports\nit, and there are also a number of mathematical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124859,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "models that don't require such an extravagantly\nbig \u0026 complex picture of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129149,
    "dDurationMs": 5241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But luckily, physics is science, not speculation,\nand eventually, someone, maybe even you, will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134390,
    "dDurationMs": 21459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perform an experiment that helps us "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155849,
    "dDurationMs": 15131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "discover the truth."
    } ]
  } ]
}
